From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: skip null buffer copy operands (STEAMAC-9S/9T)

STEAMAC-9T event 8b61b0326f434c719eaa5ea2e60644f3 faults at
kk_CmdCopyBuffer2+80, KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS 0x68. The staged driver
UUID 632D1882-1FCA-36D6-B695-FAC5EC96A7DB matches the event. Its +24
loads src/dst into x21/x22; +80 is ldp x3,x12,[x22,#0x68]. The event
has x22=0, x21=0x7993c67780 and the already-loaded source Metal buffer
x1=0x797da99a40. It is a NULL destination VkBuffer, not a NULL Metal
allocation or a non-resident sparse page. STEAMAC-9S is the supervisor's
report of the same crash. Why the guest supplied the missing handle is
not established by the report.

VkCopyBufferInfo2's srcBuffer/dstBuffer parameters are non-optional
valid VkBuffer handles (VUID-VkCopyBufferInfo2-{src,dst}Buffer-parameter).
Reject only their NULL form before recording an operation or acquiring
an encoder. Warn at most twice per process, once for each newly seen
missing operand, using a relaxed atomic bitmask. Non-NULL handles,
including fully unbound sparse-residency buffers, take the old path.
This does not attempt to validate dangling handles or freed memory.

Private release build, Metal API validation enabled:
- Before: legacy vkCmdCopyBuffer and vkCmdCopyBuffer2 each SIGSEGV
  for NULL source, destination and both (six processes).
- After: each records 1024 invalid copies, emits one bounded warning,
  then executes a valid two-region copy and checks every destination byte.
- Dense copies with nonzero memory bindings and fully unbound sparse
  read-zero/write-drop controls pass before and after, via both APIs.
Regression: host/kosmickrisp/test/copy-buffer-null.py <private dylib>
(before: add --expect-null-crashes).
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@
 #include "kosmickrisp/bridge/vk_to_mtl_map.h"
 
 #include "util/format/u_format.h"
+#include "util/log.h"
+
+#include <stdatomic.h>
 
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
 kk_CmdCopyBuffer2(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
@@ -25,6 +28,23 @@
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(kk_cmd_buffer, cmd, commandBuffer);
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(kk_buffer, src, pCopyBufferInfo->srcBuffer);
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(kk_buffer, dst, pCopyBufferInfo->dstBuffer);
+   /* Both handles are required by VkCopyBufferInfo2, also for the legacy
+    * vkCmdCopyBuffer wrapper. A sparse buffer with no resident pages still
+    * has a valid handle and must not be skipped. */
+   if (unlikely(src == NULL || dst == NULL)) {
+      static atomic_uint warned;
+      const unsigned missing = (src == NULL ? 1u : 0u) |
+                               (dst == NULL ? 2u : 0u);
+      if ((atomic_fetch_or_explicit(&warned, missing, memory_order_relaxed) &
+           missing) != missing) {
+         mesa_logw("kk: skipping invalid vkCmdCopyBuffer2: NULL buffer handle "
+                   "(src=%p dst=%p regions=%u); further warnings for these "
+                   "missing operands are suppressed",
+                   (void *)src, (void *)dst, pCopyBufferInfo->regionCount);
+      }
+      return;
+   }
+
    kk_cb_record_op(&cmd->record, KK_CB_OP_COPY);
 
    mtl_compute_encoder *encoder = cs_get_compute(cmd);
-- 
